## Outcome

Users perceived a clearer, less cluttered platform. One system now serves desktop and mobile, and it became the foundation of the mobile app. At DD360 I also shipped a guided interface tour that increased adoption and retention.

{% callout title="About metrics" %}
This project didn't measure quantitative before-and-after indicators. I'd rather say so plainly than make numbers up.
{% /callout %}

## What I learned

- **An undocumented system is debt.** Documenting from day one is what makes scaling possible.
- **Visual consistency improves perceived simplicity:** in testing, users felt more at ease when elements were consistent.
- **What I'd do differently:** define success metrics (search time, task completion) before starting, to measure before and after.
